```

### QR Code Implementation

- **Dependency**: `react-qr-code` package (already in package.json)
- **URL Generation**: Uses `window.location.origin` with fallback to deployed URL
- **Purpose**: Enable mobile testing by scanning QR codes
- **Layout**: Responsive grid that adapts to screen size

### Rules

- ✅ **DO**: Use kebab-case folder names: `onboarding`, `checkout-flow`
- ✅ **DO**: Create `_journey.ts` with proper metadata
- ✅ **DO**: Register journey in `journeys-registry.ts`
- ✅ **DO**: Update `pages` array when adding/removing pages
- ❌ **DON'T**: Use dynamic routes (`[journeyId]`)
- ❌ **DON'T**: Forget to register the journey
- ❌ **DON'T**: Hardcode journey data elsewhere

## Creating Pages

### Page Structure

Each page is a **full custom React page**:

```typescript
// src/app/prototype/journeys/onboarding/login/page.tsx
'use client';

import Link from 'next/link';
import { Box, Button, Input, Heading } from '@/components/prototype-ui';

export default function LoginPage() {
  return (
    <Box className="min-h-screen bg-bg-base p-8">
      <Heading>Login</Heading>
      <Input placeholder="Email" />
      
      {/* Links to other pages - designer controls these */}
      <Link href="/prototype/journeys/onboarding/signup">
        <Button>Create Account</Button>
      </Link>
      <Link href="/prototype/journeys/onboarding/welcome">
        <Button>Login</Button>
      </Link>
    </Box>
  );
}
```

### Key Concepts

- Pages are **fully interactive** with real navigation
- Pages can link to **any other page** (not just next/previous)
- Pages use **design system components**
- Each page is **unique and custom** (not templated)

### Rules

- ✅ **DO**: Start with `'use client';`
- ✅ **DO**: Use design system components
- ✅ **DO**: Add links to other pages using Next.js `Link`
- ✅ **DO**: Use `href` paths that match actual page locations
- ❌ **DON'T**: Use dynamic routing patterns
- ❌ **DON'T**: Create templated/generic page components

## Journey Registry

### File: `src/lib/data/journeys-registry.ts`

```typescript
import type { JourneyConfig } from '@/lib/types/journey';
import { journey as onboarding } from '@/app/prototype/journeys/onboarding/_journey';
import { journey as checkoutFlow } from '@/app/prototype/journeys/checkout-flow/_journey';

export const journeys: JourneyConfig[] = [
  onboarding,
  checkoutFlow,
];

export function getJourney(id: string): JourneyConfig | undefined {
  return journeys.find(j => j.id === id);
}

export function getAllJourneys(): JourneyConfig[] {
  return journeys;
}
```

### When to Update Registry

- Add journey: Import and add to `journeys` array
- Remove journey: Remove import and array entry

## Status Values

- `'in-progress'` - Actively being worked on (Badge: "Active")
- `'draft'` - In planning phase (Badge: "Draft")
- `'completed'` - Finished (Badge: "Completed")

## ID Format

### Rules

- ✅ **Use kebab-case**: `onboarding`, `checkout-flow`, `user-profile`
- ✅ **Match folder name**: ID must equal folder name
- ✅ **Be descriptive**: `user-profile` over `journey-04`
- ❌ **DON'T**: Use spaces or special characters
- ❌ **DON'T**: Use camelCase or PascalCase

## Overview Pages

### All Journeys Index
- **Location**: `/prototype/journeys`
- **File**: `src/app/prototype/journeys/page.tsx`
- **Uses**: `getAllJourneys()` from registry
- **Features**: 
  - Hero section with gradient background
  - Header with back button, "All Journeys" title, and navigation buttons (Canvas, Status)
  - Divider line below header
  - Description text explaining journey statuses (Active, Draft, Completed)
  - Quick stats cards showing counts by status
  - Card-based grid of all journeys with status badges

### Canvas View
- **Location**: `/canvas`
- **File**: `src/app/canvas/page.tsx`
- **Uses**: `getAllJourneys()` from registry
- **Features**: 
  - Interactive canvas with zoom controls
  - All journeys and pages displayed in a grid layout
  - Live collaboration features (cursors, comments)
  - Click any page to navigate to it

### Individual Journey
- **Location**: `/prototype/journeys/[journey-name]`
- **File**: `src/app/prototype/journeys/[journey-name]/page.tsx`
- **Uses**: Local `_journey.ts` import
- **Features**:
  - Hero section with gradient background (`bg-gradient-to-br from-success/5 via-transparent to-accent/5`)
  - Header with:
    - Left: Back button (rounded, primary) linking to `/prototype/journeys` + Journey title (size 5xl, accent color)
    - Right: Navigation buttons (Canvas, Status) matching prototype page style
    - Divider line below header (`bg-border-decorative`)
  - Description text explaining QR code usage
  - QR code grid for all pages in the journey:
    - Responsive grid: `grid-cols-3 sm:grid-cols-4 md:grid-cols-5 lg:grid-cols-6 xl:grid-cols-7`
    - Each page shows a QR code in a box with hover effects
    - Page name displayed below QR code
    - Clickable link to the actual page
    - QR codes use current origin for URL generation (with fallback to deployed URL)

## What NOT to Do

### Common Mistakes

1. **Using dynamic routes**
   - ❌ `src/app/prototype/journeys/[journeyId]/page.tsx`
   - ✅ Individual journey folders

2. **Forgetting registration**
   - ❌ Journey folder exists but not in registry
   - ✅ Always add to `journeys-registry.ts`

3. **Mismatched IDs**
   - ❌ Folder `onboarding/` but ID `onboarding-flow`
   - ✅ Folder and ID must match

4. **Wrong page paths**
   - ❌ `path: '/journeys/onboarding/login'`
   - ✅ `path: '/prototype/journeys/onboarding/login'`

5. **Dynamic/templated pages**
   - ❌ Generic `ScreenPage` component for all pages
   - ✅ Each page is custom with unique content

## Designer Workflow

1. **Plan journey**: Define pages and flow
2. **Create folder**: `src/app/prototype/journeys/[name]/`
3. **Create metadata**: `_journey.ts` with empty pages array
4. **Create pages**: Add subfolders with `page.tsx` files
5. **Update metadata**: Add pages to `pages` array
6. **Register**: Add to `journeys-registry.ts`
7. **Test**: Visit pages and verify navigation

## React Native Conversion

This static folder structure supports React Native conversion:

- **Pages**: Convert React pages to React Native screens
- **Navigation**: Replace `Link` with React Navigation
- **Components**: Convert design system components
- **Data**: Same `_journey.ts` metadata structure

When converting:
- Keep journey folder structure concept
- Use React Navigation stacks per journey
- Register screens from journey metadata

## Summary

- **Journeys = Folders**: Not dynamic routes
- **Pages = Custom**: Each page is unique
- **Registry**: Central list of all journeys
- **Navigation**: Designer controls all links
- **Metadata**: `_journey.ts` defines journey info

**Workflow:** Create folder → Add `_journey.ts` → Create pages → Register → Done!
